This file exists only so `contracts/src/` is tracked by git — Git does
not track empty directories. It has no other purpose and should be
deleted the moment the first real contract source file is added here.

Root cause this fixes: on a genuinely fresh clone (e.g. CI's checkout,
or anyone cloning this repo for the first time), `contracts/src/` did
not exist at all, because it was never actually committed — only ever
present locally, in every developer's working copy, by coincidence.
`contracts/scripts/run-slither.sh` correctly detects a missing `src/`
directory as an anomaly and fails loudly (`exit 1`) rather than silently
treating it the same as "empty but present" — which is exactly what
surfaced this. See docs/CONTRACTS_TOOLCHAIN.md.

Verified: reproduced the exact `exit 1` failure from a genuinely fresh
`git clone` (contracts/src/ did not exist; `git ls-tree` confirmed it
was never tracked), then confirmed this file resolves it.
